## What to deliver

Build and rig the mech up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: an upright body and head standing on two legs,
carrying a rifle on the right arm. **Author the two required animations** as
F-curves with the `voxel-anim` animation subcommands: `walk` (a walk whose feet
plant flat and still, then lift and swing — with weight, not a weightless slide,
the legs in opposite phase) and `fire` (a quick rifle recoil while the mech stands).
The animations are the fixed contract — produce both, by those names; the parts and
joints that realize them are yours. Before you finish, run `voxel-anim render` so it
emits the per-part `.glb` geometry your result is built from — an unrendered part is
scored as empty (`voxel-anim render --component <part>` redraws one part;
`voxel-anim render --time <ms> --animation <name>` renders the model posed at that
instant of an animation to check the motion). When you are satisfied, stop: the
recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
